WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.206
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.810
DINO CHIESA: Hi, Dino here.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:12.120
In this video, we will get to
know Apigee's API analytics.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.990
There are three big pieces
to managing an API program--

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:20.340
exposing your APIs, enabling
others to consume your APIs,

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.170
and then measuring
that activity.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.720
APIs are foundational
for digital business,

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.960
so it's very important to
have complete visibility

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.500
into API performance.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.970
You want to track developer
usage, API usage trends, error

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.060
rates, geographic distribution.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.700
All of these metrics and
more are available to you

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.740
through the Apigee
Edge platform so you

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:47.620
can analyze your digital
business in real time.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.370
Let me show you some
of what you get.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.710
Navigate to the analytics
menu on the left-hand side.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:56.110
Let's take a look.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:59.470
The API proxy
performance chart will

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:03.550
show traffic volumes and
response times for your APIs.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.130
This is such valuable insight.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:09.460
Some customers create an Apigee
pass-through proxy on existing

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.500
services just to get this view.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.160
You can view data for a
specific proxy or all proxies.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.700
Look back an hour, a
day, a week, or more.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.020
And it's built-in.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:28.300
You don't have to do anything
to get this, so nice.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.150
This report can be a great
resource for your developers

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.170
and DevOps team.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.120
The cache performance
chart shows

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.950
utilization of the
built-in Apigee Edge

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.930
cache for your APIs.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.660
This is really handy
for helping to optimize

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.482
performance and efficiency.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:52.480
The geomap shows you the
geographic source of traffic.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:56.380
It's marvelous to be able to
track API proxy usage by geo

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.570
to see where usage originates.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.990
The latency analysis
chart is invaluable

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.230
when managing to a
response time goal.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:12.540
Stable performance is key for
a quality user experience.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:19.260
This Apigee chart shows
TP 50, TP 95, and TP 99.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.780
That's average response
time as well as

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:25.540
95th and 99th percentile.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.880
When you have
spikes in TP 99, it

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.890
indicates that other
pieces in your system

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.950
are not delivering stable
performance under load.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.960
This chart pinpoints
that problem.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.960
The traffic composition report
shows you the top proxies,

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:46.250
products, apps, or developers
by traffic volumes,

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:49.250
obviously valuable when
managing an API program.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.860
And you can create
your own custom reports

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.690
based on the
individual metrics that

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:03.090
are collected by Apigee Edge,
like latency, IP address, path,

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.680
and response status code.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.270
This is just a quick sample.

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:14.270
To get these charts for your
traffic, all you need to do

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.720
is create an API proxy in
Apigee Edge and direct client

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.730
applications to use it.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.070
And of course, all of the
data presented visually

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:25.250
in these charts is
available via an API,

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:29.660
so you can export it into
your own analysis tools.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.760
OK, that's the
quick introduction

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.710
to Apigee Edge analytics.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:36.650
It gives you visibility into
key performance and operating

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.190
metrics for your APIs.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.350
And if you want to know
more, dive into the product

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:44.740
documentation or
visit the community.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.540
Until next time,
keep it digital.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:49.890
[MUSIC PLAYING]

